Translation patch: `Params::into_values`, `Params::into_positional`, `From<Vec<(N, V)>> for Params` (`HashMap`)

Change: The `HashMap<Vec<u8>, Value>` of `Params::Named` is only used through `sql_trusted` (patch 80):
  - `into_values`: `for (name, value) in map` becomes `for (name, value) in sql_trusted::params_map_into_entries(map)` (the entries collected into a `Vec` in the map's iteration order).
  - `into_positional`: the loop `'params: for (i, name) in named_params.iter().enumerate() { match map.entry(name.clone()) { Occupied(entry) => { <scan x from len-1 down to i+1 for named_params[x] == name: if found, push entry.get().clone() and continue 'params> push entry.remove() } _ => return Err(..) } }` becomes an index loop (`while i < named_params.len()`) that first does the same scan into a flag `repeated` (stopping at the first match, as before), then, if `repeated`, `match params_map_get(&map, name) { Some(v) => push v.clone(), None => return Err(..) }`, else `match params_map_remove(&mut map, name) { Some(v) => push v, None => return Err(..) }`.
  - `From<Vec<(N, V)>>`: `HashMap::default()` becomes `params_map_new()`, and `match map.entry(name) { Vacant(e) => e.insert(Value::from(value)), Occupied(_) => panic!(..) }` becomes `if params_map_contains_key(&map, &name) { panic!(..) } else { params_map_insert(&mut map, name, Value::from(value)); }`.
  - The now unused `Entry` imports are dropped.
Why: `HashMap` is a std type Aeneas does not model; `sql_trusted` is the opaque trust boundary. Aeneas does not model `Enumerate`, the slice iterator or labelled `continue` out of a nested loop (patches 04/05/27).
Behaviour: Identical:
  - `into_values` visits the same entries in the same order (`into_iter().collect()` into a `Vec` and then iterating the `Vec` yields the map's iteration sequence).
  - `into_positional`: the scan for a later equal name reads only `named_params`, so doing it before the map lookup instead of after it changes nothing; `get`/`remove` return `None` exactly when `entry` was `Vacant` (the key is absent), giving the same `Err`; otherwise the same value is cloned or removed. `name.clone()` as the `entry` key was only a lookup key. `named_params.len() - 1` is only evaluated inside the loop, where `len >= 1`, as before.
  - `From<Vec<(N, V)>>`: the name is converted first, as before; if it is already present we panic before converting the value (as the `Occupied` arm did); otherwise `Value::from(value)` is evaluated and inserted under the key, as `Vacant::insert` did.

